{"text": "From: delaRosa, Mark (CON)\n\nTo: Dioins. Massanda (CON); Sobrepena, Amanda (CON); Chalk, Kate (CON); Basnet, Snehi (CON); Oo, Todd\nwa\nce: Moo econ\n\u2018Subject: RE: Community Benefits Aut\nDate: \u201cTuesday, October 27, 2020 1:35:41 PM\n\nThanks, team!\n\nMark de la Rosa\n\u2018Acting Director of Audits\nOffice of the Controller, City Services Auditor\nCity and County of San Francisco\n(415) 554-7574\nmark.p.delarosa@sfaov.org\n\nFrom: Djohns, Massanda (CON) <massanda.djohns@sfgov.org>\nSent: Tuesday, October 27, 2020 12:35 PM\nTo: delaRosa, Mark (CON) <mark.p.delarosa@sfgov.org>; Sobrepena, Amanda (CON)\n<amanda.sobrepena@sfgov.org>; Chalk, Kate (CON) <kate.chalk@sfgov.org>; Basnet, Snehi (CON)\n<snehibasnet@sfgov.org>; Ojo, Todd (CON) <todd.ojo@sfgov.org>; Zywno, Joanna (CON)\n<joanna.zywno@sfgov.ore>; Scoggin, Kathleen (CON) <kathleen.scoggin@sfgov.ore>; Jensen, Dave\n(CON) <dave.a.jensen@sfgov.org>; Tipton, Mark (CON) <mark.tipton@sfgov.org>; Ho, Nelson (CON)\n<nelson.ho@sfgov.org>\nCe: Woo, Winnie (CON) <winnie. woo@sfgov.org>\nSubject: RE: Community Benefits Audit\n\n\u2018Amanda,\nYes, thank you for the backdrop.\nMark,\n\nOne addition, is that in my biweekly updates to Matt Low, | informed him back in July that the\nExternal Affairs Audit (name on our work plan) and the Community Benefits Audits were not two\ndistinct audits. We would discuss further the audit in late Q2. My communications to Matt Low have\nalso been vague given any potential impact due to Pl on the nature or timing of the audit.\n\nRegards,\nMassanda\n\nMassanda D'Johns\n\nLead Manager\nOffice of the Controller - City Services Auditor\n1 Dr. Carlton B. Goodlett Place - City Hall Room 382",
